<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="F_ValidReqID" Id="{da241a71-d251-4194-bb1e-c62816f4a193}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_ValidReqID - may this request/assertion ID be used as an assertion key?

    PURPOSE
        Decide whether a request/assertion ID handed to the beam-parameter
        transition manager (BPTM) is a usable key for the arbiter's assertion
        pool. Exactly two values of the DWORD input are rejected:
            0        - no ID assigned (the BPTM input defaults to 0)
            16#FFFFFFFF (PMPS_GVL.EXCLUDED_ASSERTION_ID)
                     - reserved sentinel that must never match an assertion
        Every other DWORD value is accepted.

    USAGE
        Called from the SetNewTarget action of BeamParameterTransitionManager,
        on both IDs it is about to install:
            IF F_ValidReqID(i_nRequestedAssertionID) AND
                F_ValidReqID(i_TransitionAssertionID) THEN
        and again in the failure branch to pick the error code
        (PMPS_CODES.BadTargetID for the requested ID, PMPS_CODES.BadTransID
        for the transition ID). Both BPTM inputs are UDINT and are passed
        unchanged to the DWORD input below.
        The function is pure - it reads only its input and that one GVL
        constant, keeps no state and has no side effects - so it may be called
        from any task, from production code and from test code.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Give "a valid request ID" one definition, so the exclusion of 0 and
          of the sentinel is written once instead of at every call site.
        - Keep both sentinel values out of the arbiter: FB_Arbiter.AddRequest
          refuses the same two IDs, so a caller that skips this check cannot
          install a request the arbiter would then be unable to look up.
        - Turn a bad ID into a distinct, logged error at the BPTM instead of a
          request that silently never asserts.

    RETURNS
        BOOL - TRUE when ReqID may be used as an assertion ID, FALSE for one of
        the two rejected values. FALSE is the safe answer: the caller raises a
        fault instead of requesting beam.

    NOTES
        - Only the two sentinel values are rejected here. Whether an ID is
          already present in the pool is a separate question, asked with
          FB_Arbiter.CheckRequestInPool; uniqueness stays the caller's job.
        - IDs are compared as unsigned 32-bit values; nothing in this function
          range-checks, hashes or stores the ID.

    HISTORY
        2020-08-18 / Alex Wallace
            Function added with the BPTM change that made the transition
            manager reject bad transition IDs (commit 1472f04).
        2024-01-29 / ghalym
            Reformatted by pre-commit; logic unchanged (commit 1335761).
        2026-09-16 / Yann Stephen Mandza
            XAE ProductVersion attribute removed from the TcPlcObject element
            (commit f77073f).
        2026-11-28 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header and the ReqID comment; documentation only, no
            behaviour change (audit finding #270, conv_321640e095c0).
*)
FUNCTION F_ValidReqID : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    ReqID : DWORD; // Request/assertion ID to validate: the key the caller wants to put in
                   // the arbiter's assertion pool. No units. 0 (no ID assigned) and
                   // 16#FFFFFFFF (PMPS_GVL.EXCLUDED_ASSERTION_ID, the never-matches
                   // sentinel) are rejected; any other DWORD value is accepted.
END_VAR
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[F_ValidReqID := ReqID <> PMPS_GVL.EXCLUDED_ASSERTION_ID AND ReqID <> 0;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>